{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Rice Cookout", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Cooking up a Storm", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Pronunciation of Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Where do you put the stress in a phrasal verb?", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If the phrasal verb needs an object, or is not separable, then you stress the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with</span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">go</span> along</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">How long have you been <span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with food and cooking?</span> (taken with - is not finished without the objects food and cooking)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Let's <span class=\"strong\">go</span> along here.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the phrasal verb is separable, then the stress is on the particle (preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\">whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span></span><br/><span class=\"italic\">I'll whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span> a rice dish. <br/>I'll whip a rice dish <span class=\"strong\">up</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Let's <span class=\"strong\">go</span> along here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've <span class=\"strong\">been</span> into cooking in a big way.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been <span class=\"strong\">reading</span> up on the different types of rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How long have you been <span class=\"strong\">taken</span> with food and cooking?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've never tried one <span class=\"strong\">out</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I could use it to whip <span class=\"strong\">up</span> rice dishes quickly and efficiently.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have a recipe for squid that's chopped <span class=\"strong\">up</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Acorn squash hollowed <span class=\"strong\">out</span> and filled with zucchini and rice is a nice staple.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Pronouncing the Letters  <span class=\"italic\">squ</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When two or more consonants are used together they can make a new sound - a <span class=\"strong\">consonant blend</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In words with <span class=\"italic\">squ</span>, you blend the <span class=\"strong\">s</span> sound and the <span class=\"strong\">qu</span> (kw) to make the <span class=\"strong\">squ</span> (skw) sound as in <span class=\"italic\">squid</span> and <span class=\"italic\">squelch</span>. Note that <span class=\"strong\">sq</span> is always followed by <span class=\"strong\">u</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say these words out loud. Notice the blending of the sounds /s/ and /kw/.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squid\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwid)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"square\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skware)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squirt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwirt)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squab\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwab)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squishy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwishy)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squeamish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skweemish)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squeeze\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skweez)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"squash\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(skwash)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Now try saying these sentences out loud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Squishy seafood!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Squid makes me squeamish.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Don't they squirt black ink?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have a recipe for squid that's chopped up.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could walk along the Charles starting at Kendal Square.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to whip up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make quickly and easily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's whip up a nice dessert.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when talk about cooking squid.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "squid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sea animal with a long body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a recipe for squid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to chop up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cut into pieces", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Please chop up the vegetables.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mix with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to combine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The vegetables mixed with fried rice looks delicious!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "squeamish", "type": "name"}, {"c